WEBVTT

00:12.047 --> 00:15.307
Webster's defines "class"
as "a group of students

00:15.317 --> 00:19.211
gathered at a pre-ordained time
for the purposes of education."

00:19.221 --> 00:22.447
Angela pretty much epitomized class.

00:22.457 --> 00:26.017
Who could turn the world on
with her smile? Angela.

00:26.027 --> 00:27.552
Who could take a nothing day

00:27.562 --> 00:31.123
and suddenly make it all
seem worthwhile? Angela.

00:31.133 --> 00:34.390
So no one told you life
was gonna be this way.

00:35.604 --> 00:36.928
Angela.

00:36.938 --> 00:40.866
Sometimes you want to go
where everybody knows your name.

00:40.876 --> 00:42.167
Angela.

00:47.282 --> 00:48.607
Angela.

00:48.617 --> 00:51.076
I'm sorry. Death is hard for me.

00:51.086 --> 00:53.845
But at least Angela died
doing what she loved:

00:53.855 --> 00:56.815
swimming less than 20 minutes
after she had eaten.

00:56.825 --> 00:59.518
That's a real thing, kids.
Listen to your mothers.

00:59.528 --> 01:03.321
That was Angela. Fearless. Spontaneous.

01:03.331 --> 01:06.358
Honest, about herself
just as much as she was

01:06.368 --> 01:08.260
about the world around her.

01:08.270 --> 01:12.931
She had grace, courage,
and an unmatched zest for life.

01:12.941 --> 01:15.734
She may be gone,
but her voice will live on

01:15.744 --> 01:18.136
in DVD and Hulu Plus

01:18.146 --> 01:21.373
and tiny droid-projected messages.

01:21.383 --> 01:23.842
I may have lost a boss,

01:23.852 --> 01:26.854
but heaven has gained a princess.

01:30.192 --> 01:32.726
And I am at the wrong funeral.

01:34.729 --> 01:38.523
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

01:38.533 --> 01:41.893
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

01:41.903 --> 01:45.564
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

01:45.574 --> 01:48.466
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

01:48.476 --> 01:51.903
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

01:51.913 --> 01:55.307
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

01:55.317 --> 01:56.908
<i>All the things that make us</i>

01:56.918 --> 01:58.710
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

01:58.720 --> 02:04.123
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

02:10.098 --> 02:12.090
Any idea what this meeting is about?

02:15.437 --> 02:18.530
Oh, we're getting a new boss?
Oh, I hope it's Hugo Boss.

02:18.540 --> 02:20.098
Then we'll all look snazzy.

02:20.108 --> 02:21.566
<i>Tonight's episode of Family Guy</i>

02:21.576 --> 02:23.535
<i>is brought to you by Hugo Boss.</i>

02:23.545 --> 02:25.737
<i>Look for us in the
low-trafficked corner of Macy's</i>

02:25.747 --> 02:28.940
<i>between Eddie Bauer and
the never-bought male jewelry.</i>

02:28.950 --> 02:32.110
Attention, everyone!
Do not adjust your TV sets.

02:32.120 --> 02:34.412
We are an interracial couple.

02:34.422 --> 02:36.081
I'd like to introduce myself.

02:36.091 --> 02:39.417
My name is Bert and this
is my lovely wife Sheila.

02:39.427 --> 02:42.287
Two sets of disappointed parents
right there.

02:42.297 --> 02:44.522
- Well, only her parents.
- Aah!

02:44.532 --> 02:46.558
Now that Angela's no longer with us,

02:46.568 --> 02:48.526
we will be your new bosses.

02:48.536 --> 02:50.562
We're splitting the job
because one of the shareholders'

02:50.572 --> 02:53.298
favorite songs was "Ebony and Ivory,"

02:53.308 --> 02:55.800
so here we are.

02:55.810 --> 02:57.736
Now we know it's difficult to remember

02:57.746 --> 03:00.138
two new names, so to make things easier,

03:00.148 --> 03:02.774
- you can call us "Beila."
- Or "Shert."

03:04.653 --> 03:06.912
Boy, I bet you
she's a handful in the bedroom.

03:06.922 --> 03:08.280
Two handfuls, baby.

03:08.290 --> 03:10.315
Damn it, I went all the way
around the room!

03:10.325 --> 03:12.484
Now, some of you may find the idea

03:12.494 --> 03:15.453
of two bosses unconventional, but...

03:15.463 --> 03:18.456
We assure you nothing will be different.

03:18.466 --> 03:24.095
And our door will always be open
to you any time of day.

03:24.105 --> 03:28.833
And there is no issue
too big or too small.

03:28.843 --> 03:31.569
Nice to meet all of you.

03:31.579 --> 03:34.673
So, as our mascot Pawtucket Pat says,

03:34.683 --> 03:38.285
"All ye Federalists, imbibe!"

03:40.021 --> 03:41.913
It means, "Everybody, drink."

03:41.923 --> 03:43.181
Yay!

03:43.191 --> 03:45.968
Two bosses? This sucks.

03:45.978 --> 03:47.933
Well, at least it beats
being home with my wife.

03:47.943 --> 03:48.951
Peter!

03:48.961 --> 03:51.254
Aah! When did we cut back home?

03:57.038 --> 03:58.964
- Hey, Peter.
- All right, Sheila,

03:58.974 --> 04:01.366
let's do it right here
on the desk while Bert watches.

04:01.376 --> 04:03.301
No, Peter, that's not what this is.

04:03.311 --> 04:05.370
Sorry, I-I thought
I was picking up on a vibe.

04:05.380 --> 04:08.139
So, Peter, we've been tasked
with making the operations

04:08.149 --> 04:10.709
around here run more efficiently,

04:10.719 --> 04:13.712
and part of that will involve
reassigning people

04:13.722 --> 04:15.347
based on their abilities.

04:15.357 --> 04:18.216
We want you to be
the office recyclables guy.

04:18.226 --> 04:20.185
So we're gonna put a flag on you,

04:20.195 --> 04:21.953
and wherever you go, people will know

04:21.963 --> 04:24.398
that's where they put their recyclables.

04:26.101 --> 04:28.202
Please don't just throw them over.

04:30.405 --> 04:32.697
Well, at least make sure all
the liquids are gone, please,

04:32.707 --> 04:34.408
before you throw them.

04:36.211 --> 04:38.903
Smithers, who is that young go-getter?

04:38.913 --> 04:41.172
That's a character
from another show, sir.

04:41.182 --> 04:43.775
- Simpson, you say?
- Pretty much, sir. mu

04:48.523 --> 04:50.749
<i>We now return to Titanic 2,</i>

04:50.759 --> 04:52.426
<i>narrated by Al Gore.</i>

04:54.262 --> 04:56.521
Iceberg, right ahead!

04:56.531 --> 05:00.525
<i>But due to man's
excessive use of fossil fuels,</i>

05:00.535 --> 05:02.660
<i>climate change had rendered the iceberg</i>

05:02.670 --> 05:05.472
nothing more than a small cube.

05:07.675 --> 05:09.934
Peter, why are you wearing a flag?

05:09.944 --> 05:12.604
Eh, it's part of my job now
'cause of my new bosses.

05:12.614 --> 05:14.539
Uh, is it a promotion?

05:14.549 --> 05:16.541
Because it doesn't
look like a promotion.

05:16.551 --> 05:18.943
No, it looks like an old lady's Rascal.

05:18.953 --> 05:21.379
- Aah!
- So, who are these new bosses?

05:21.389 --> 05:24.649
Their names are Bert and Sheila.
My job sucks now.

05:24.659 --> 05:27.018
It's worse than when
I was a dinosaur walker.

05:27.028 --> 05:29.988
- Hey!
- What?

05:29.998 --> 05:31.790
- Pick that up!
- Pick what up?

05:31.800 --> 05:33.825
- That!
- That? That was there.

05:33.835 --> 05:35.593
No, you were looking at your phone.

05:35.603 --> 05:37.228
- No, I wasn't.
- Yes, you were.

05:37.238 --> 05:38.596
Sir, this is a neighborhood

05:38.606 --> 05:40.632
where we respect the rules of society.

05:40.642 --> 05:43.429
Ooh! Society now.
Sir Thomas More up here.

05:43.439 --> 05:44.647
Good for you and your neighborhood.

05:44.657 --> 05:46.304
I'm gonna take a picture of you
and post it on Facebook.

05:46.314 --> 05:48.406
Oh, great!
I hope it gets a lot of likes.

05:48.416 --> 05:49.808
You know what? I forgot my bag.

05:49.818 --> 05:52.085
- Ooh, you forgot your bag?
- Yeah, I forgot my bag.

05:52.095 --> 05:53.140
But I'll be sure to come back

05:53.150 --> 05:54.633
- and pick this up.
- Oh, yes, I'm sure you'll be back.

05:54.643 --> 05:56.781
Look, I'm only here to create
an amusing comparison

05:56.791 --> 05:58.349
- to my current job...
- Well, bully for you.

05:58.359 --> 05:59.651
Which I am, at this moment,

05:59.661 --> 06:01.126
describing to my family
in my living room.

06:01.136 --> 06:03.154
So, technically, you don't even exist.

06:03.164 --> 06:05.623
Well, how do you know I wasn't
telling my wife a story

06:05.633 --> 06:07.826
and you're a figment of my imagination?

06:07.836 --> 06:10.328
I-I can assure you that is not the case.

06:10.338 --> 06:13.164
<i>We'll be right back
with more Greg in the Window.</i>

06:13.174 --> 06:14.632
Well, I'll be.

06:14.642 --> 06:16.634
<i>Window!</i>

06:16.644 --> 06:18.803
<i>Greg in the Window, brought to you by</i>

06:18.813 --> 06:20.814
<i>never-bought male jewelry.</i>

06:24.686 --> 06:28.012
Okay, Peter, we've got
something else for you.

06:28.022 --> 06:31.749
We need you to taste test our
new varieties of seasonal beers,

06:31.759 --> 06:33.952
which will be coming down
this conveyor belt.

06:33.962 --> 06:35.587
Place those on this tray.

06:35.597 --> 06:37.155
All right, that seems easy enough.

06:37.165 --> 06:38.823
Also, our delivery truck drivers

06:38.833 --> 06:40.825
have to pass an annual drug test,

06:40.835 --> 06:43.294
so we'll need you to collect
their urine samples.

06:43.304 --> 06:45.330
They'll be coming down
this same conveyor belt

06:45.340 --> 06:47.165
in similarly colored cups,

06:47.175 --> 06:49.501
which you will need to place
on this tray.

06:49.511 --> 06:50.935
Well, that doesn't seem like a...

06:50.945 --> 06:52.537
<i>Belt activated.</i>

06:52.547 --> 06:55.507
Uh, showtime.

06:57.519 --> 06:59.777
Pumpkin, not bad.

06:59.787 --> 07:02.419
Ugh, trucker pee.

07:02.429 --> 07:04.482
<i>Belt speed increasing.</i>

07:04.492 --> 07:05.650
Oh, boy.

07:05.660 --> 07:08.453
Apple cinnamon, not bad.

07:08.463 --> 07:10.355
Pee laced with meth.

07:10.365 --> 07:13.664
- Winter wheat.
- Lady trucker pee.

07:14.696 --> 07:16.361
<i>Belt speed maximum.</i>

07:16.371 --> 07:19.330
Ah, crap! Trucker. Trucker.

07:19.340 --> 07:21.499
Oktoberfest. Trucker.

07:21.509 --> 07:25.336
Amber squash, yuck. Trucker. Trucker.

07:25.346 --> 07:28.215
And let's hope this one
was an Asparagus IPA.

07:32.887 --> 07:35.580
Too bad about the latest
sales numbers, huh?

07:35.590 --> 07:38.216
I don't talk to anyone
standing at a urinal.

07:38.226 --> 07:40.718
Too bad about the latest
sales numbers, huh?

07:40.728 --> 07:41.886
Thanks for waiting.

07:41.896 --> 07:43.821
You know, our testing
came back and shows

07:43.831 --> 07:45.423
we're losing market share.

07:45.433 --> 07:48.726
Apparently, nobody can relate
to our mascot Pawtucket Pat.

07:48.736 --> 07:50.828
Are you guys
talking about work in there?

07:50.838 --> 07:53.731
Oh, yes, come on in, honey.
We've put our wangs away.

07:53.741 --> 07:55.700
Did you tell him about our testing?

07:55.710 --> 07:58.636
Yeah, our customers find
a 300-year-old mascot

07:58.646 --> 08:01.973
hard to relate to,
they want a regular guy.

08:01.983 --> 08:05.843
You know, a-a guy who'd
drink a beer on a toilet.

08:08.056 --> 08:09.681
Griffin?

08:09.691 --> 08:10.982
No.

08:10.992 --> 08:12.796
It is you, Peter.

08:12.806 --> 08:13.957
What are you doing?

08:13.967 --> 08:16.254
Playing a game on my phone
and having a beer.

08:16.264 --> 08:17.956
And, God willing, going to the bathroom.

08:17.966 --> 08:19.924
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

08:19.934 --> 08:22.093
He must be (BLEEP) on his shirt tail?

08:22.103 --> 08:24.028
Ew, yes, but also,

08:24.038 --> 08:25.830
that's exactly the kind of customer

08:25.840 --> 08:27.432
we should be appealing to.

08:27.442 --> 08:30.768
I think we found our new mascot.
Are you in, Peter?

08:31.669 --> 08:34.105
May I have a moment
to talk it over with my mentor?

08:34.115 --> 08:35.773
Sure.

08:38.953 --> 08:41.613
I'm in.

08:41.623 --> 08:44.088
<i>No. We did it.</i>

08:50.328 --> 08:52.921
Wow, Peter, so you're really
replacing Pawtucket Pat

08:52.931 --> 08:56.091
- as the new mascot?
- Yup, I'm the new Pawtucket Pat.

08:56.101 --> 08:57.993
Hey, now you and Jared from Subway

08:58.003 --> 08:59.494
have two things in common.

08:59.504 --> 09:02.497
No! No, that's not true, Meg!
It's not true!

09:02.507 --> 09:04.332
Peter, Peter, she's garbage.
She's garbage.

09:04.342 --> 09:07.502
- Let it go. You're the king.
- Yeah, garbage, yeah.

09:07.512 --> 09:08.870
Anyway, turn on the TV.

09:08.880 --> 09:10.842
They're about to play
my first commercial.

09:38.543 --> 09:40.202
<i>Pawtucket Patriot:</i>

09:40.212 --> 09:42.871
<i>the perfect beer
for New England beaches.</i>

09:48.887 --> 09:51.112
Ladies and gentlemen,

09:51.122 --> 09:53.882
throwing out today's
ceremonial first pitch,

09:53.892 --> 09:56.818
the face of
the Pawtucket Patriot Brewery,

09:56.828 --> 09:58.829
Pawtucket Pat!

10:07.239 --> 10:10.532
Aah! Please kill me!

10:10.542 --> 10:12.367
Still buy the beer, though.

10:12.377 --> 10:16.071
And now, a five-hour baseball game.

10:16.081 --> 10:17.572
Hey, guys, I'm Billy on the Street,

10:17.582 --> 10:19.341
and I'm here with
one of the biggest mascots

10:19.351 --> 10:22.210
- in America right now.
- Popular, he means. Not large.

10:22.220 --> 10:23.545
Let me do my intro!

10:23.555 --> 10:25.981
Okay, we're gonna go up
to people and give a dollar

10:25.991 --> 10:28.216
to everyone who recognizes you.
Let's go.

10:28.226 --> 10:31.052
Sir, sir, sir, for a dollar,
do you know who this is?

10:31.062 --> 10:33.421
- No.
- Oh, come on, he's in a new commercial.

10:33.431 --> 10:34.923
I don't even own a TV.

10:34.933 --> 10:38.260
Oh, you don't own a TV?
I'm very impressed! Let's go!

10:38.270 --> 10:40.128
Sir, sir, quick, tell me.

10:40.138 --> 10:41.796
- Who is this man?
- Uh...

10:41.806 --> 10:44.599
<i>Adweek magazine called him
the Pitchman of the Year.</i>

10:44.609 --> 10:46.434
<i>Who doesn't read Adweek?!</i>

10:46.444 --> 10:48.136
There's, uh, there's more running

10:48.146 --> 10:49.704
than I thought there'd be.

10:49.714 --> 10:52.307
- Oh, is he Jerry Ferrara?
- Jerry Ferrara?

10:52.317 --> 10:55.076
<i>You mean Turtle from Entourage?
You're the worst!</i>

10:55.086 --> 10:56.778
<i>Even worse than the Entourage movie!</i>

10:56.788 --> 11:00.015
Mark Wahlberg is one of
our finest producers!

11:00.025 --> 11:03.396
I-I don't, uh, I-I don't feel
comfortable doing this.

11:03.406 --> 11:05.453
He was just getting a cup
of coffee with his daughter.

11:05.463 --> 11:08.156
- They should know you!
- Hey, you're Pawtucket Pat.

11:08.166 --> 11:10.559
Yes, thank you! He's Pawtucket Pat!

11:10.569 --> 11:11.693
Not that I watch this show.

11:11.703 --> 11:14.763
<i>I watch Black Mirror and
The Goldbergs, and that's it!</i>

11:14.773 --> 11:16.731
Wow, can I get a picture with you?

11:16.741 --> 11:19.100
- No!
- What's his problem?

11:19.110 --> 11:21.803
Between you and me, I think
he may need a lady friend.

11:21.813 --> 11:23.638
Peter, I'm famously gay!

11:23.648 --> 11:26.250
Oh, my God, he ran around the world.

11:31.456 --> 11:33.729
Hey, so how's the whole
Pawtucket Pat thing going?

11:33.739 --> 11:34.823
Aw, it's the best.

11:34.833 --> 11:37.486
Everywhere I go,
people recognize me and love me.

11:37.496 --> 11:39.267
And the other day,
I even got to hang out

11:39.277 --> 11:41.323
with a bunch of other famous mascots.

11:41.333 --> 11:44.125
So, you, uh, you really make
all those cookies in that tree?

11:44.135 --> 11:46.227
- They're great!
- Like, the tree is wood.

11:46.237 --> 11:48.296
Like, how does the tree
not catch on fire?

11:48.306 --> 11:50.332
Hey, you want to cool it
with that drumming?

11:50.342 --> 11:52.400
Anyway, do you have to water your house?

11:52.410 --> 11:53.702
- 'Cause I would think that...
- They're great!

11:53.712 --> 11:55.437
You know what, let's just forget
the conversation

11:55.447 --> 11:57.031
and just pose for the picture.

11:57.949 --> 12:00.275
By the way, Tony,
I'm sorry your wife was shot

12:00.285 --> 12:02.286
by Donald Trump's children.

12:06.558 --> 12:10.018
Hi, Peter.
It's me, Sheila, and me, Bert.

12:10.028 --> 12:12.821
Here's a dollar! Stop talking like that!

12:12.831 --> 12:14.622
Sorry about him. We ruined people's days

12:14.632 --> 12:15.957
in New York earlier.

12:15.967 --> 12:18.164
We came by to share some great news.

12:18.174 --> 12:20.628
That's right.
Your character's so popular,

12:20.638 --> 12:24.580
you're gonna have a balloon
in the annual Quahog Parade!

12:24.590 --> 12:27.783
- No way. That's awesome!
- Said no one ever.

12:27.793 --> 12:29.886
Ah. Yes. I've seen that on the Internet.

12:29.896 --> 12:31.254
Uh, who is this?

12:31.264 --> 12:33.289
Oh, that's-that's my dog, Brian.

12:33.299 --> 12:35.525
You have a dog that makes jokes
and drinks beer?

12:35.535 --> 12:37.126
Not just any beer.

12:37.136 --> 12:39.161
Pawtucket Patriot Truckers Blend.

12:39.171 --> 12:42.532
- Ah, I approved that.
- Oh, this is just what we need.

12:42.542 --> 12:45.001
- You guys are great together.
- What are you talking about?

12:45.011 --> 12:48.971
Well, think about it, Peter.
The public loves Pawtucket Pat.

12:48.981 --> 12:51.240
Imagine how much they'd love to know

12:51.250 --> 12:54.610
he has a funny sidekick dog
who drinks with him.

12:54.620 --> 12:57.446
Wow, that could be really cool.
What do you say, Brian?

12:57.456 --> 12:59.549
You're saying you need
a mascot's sidekick?

12:59.559 --> 13:01.050
Hold my beer.

13:01.060 --> 13:03.528
Uhp, that's also from the Internet.

13:09.402 --> 13:11.561
Hi, I'm Bert of Bert and Sheila.

13:11.571 --> 13:12.895
And I'm Sheila.

13:12.905 --> 13:15.164
All right. Now, before
we bring out Daughtry...

13:15.174 --> 13:18.568
Hurry it up!
Some of us came for Daughtry!

13:18.578 --> 13:21.904
It's our pleasure
to introduce Pawtucket Pat

13:21.914 --> 13:24.874
and his new sidekick Hops McElaney,

13:24.884 --> 13:28.177
the Alcoholic Dog. Come on, y'all!

13:30.256 --> 13:31.914
- Say, Brian...
- "Hops."

13:31.924 --> 13:33.494
- Hops.
- Yes, Peter?

13:33.504 --> 13:34.517
- "Pat."
- Pat.

13:34.527 --> 13:36.852
What were you doing
up on the roof last night?

13:36.862 --> 13:38.354
- Well, Peter...
- "Pat."

13:38.364 --> 13:40.022
Pat. I was up on the roof

13:40.032 --> 13:42.592
because you told me
drinks were on the house.

13:44.937 --> 13:46.262
Nice one, Brian.

13:46.272 --> 13:47.430
- "Hops."
- Hops.

13:47.440 --> 13:49.198
Let's hear more from the dog!

13:49.208 --> 13:50.633
Hops! Hops! Hops!

13:50.643 --> 13:53.278
And Daughtry!

13:56.782 --> 13:59.442
I'm sorry, sir, you can't park here.

13:59.452 --> 14:01.444
This spot is reserved
for the brewery mascot.

14:01.454 --> 14:03.245
Yeah, I am the brewery mascot.

14:03.255 --> 14:06.266
No, you're the brewery mascot's
sidekick.

14:09.929 --> 14:12.321
<i>What the hell? I'm the sidekick?</i>

14:12.331 --> 14:14.624
Aw, my life can't get any worse.

14:14.634 --> 14:16.359
Hey, at least
you're not getting attacked

14:16.369 --> 14:18.060
by a goose for no reason.

14:18.070 --> 14:20.262
Hey, you got bread, bro?
Give me that bread, bro.

14:20.272 --> 14:21.597
Come on, bro. Bro.

14:21.607 --> 14:24.204
Help me, Officer Goosefear!

14:31.237 --> 14:33.729
Guys, from now on,
I need to stand this up

14:33.739 --> 14:35.264
in the middle of your table.

14:35.274 --> 14:38.167
Pawww yeah!

14:38.177 --> 14:40.169
'Cause he's a dog.

14:40.179 --> 14:43.072
Man, I hate being a sidekick
to this stupid dog.

14:43.082 --> 14:45.674
- Yeah, I can imagine, Peter.
- I doubt you can, Quagmire.

14:45.684 --> 14:47.109
None of you can.

14:47.119 --> 14:49.044
- Well, I think I understand...
- I'm talking, Glenn.

14:49.054 --> 14:51.347
I doubt any of you can begin
to know what it's like

14:51.357 --> 14:53.015
to ride someone's coattails,

14:53.025 --> 14:55.150
to play second fiddle to some fat idiot,

14:55.160 --> 14:57.253
to constantly be setting up
someone else's...

14:57.263 --> 15:00.022
<i>It's The Joe Show</i>

15:00.032 --> 15:02.491
<i>Starring Joe</i>

15:02.501 --> 15:04.660
<i>Doing all sorts of Joe things</i>

15:04.670 --> 15:09.173
<i>Not your average Joe,
and also he can walk.</i>

15:10.993 --> 15:13.903
Just a footnote
to someone else's narrative.

15:13.913 --> 15:15.271
I tell you, this sucks worse

15:15.281 --> 15:17.373
than being a monkey at Coachella.

15:17.383 --> 15:20.476
Dude, it sucks this year.
There's no good bands.

15:20.486 --> 15:23.593
- There's Bananarama.
- There's, like, one good band.

15:27.672 --> 15:30.138
Hey, Brian, you want to go to the park?

15:30.148 --> 15:31.220
The public park?

15:31.230 --> 15:33.822
Uh, no, I don't think
that'd be a good idea.

15:33.832 --> 15:34.957
Because of Beaglemania.

15:34.967 --> 15:36.659
- What?
- My fame.

15:36.669 --> 15:39.862
- That's what they're calling it.
- Who's calling it Beaglemania?

15:39.872 --> 15:42.398
Well, you just did. Catching on.

15:42.408 --> 15:44.400
Well, leave it to you to ruin it.

15:44.410 --> 15:47.202
Just like Dasani ruined water.

15:47.212 --> 15:51.006
Hey, guys, so you know
how water tastes like nothing?

15:51.016 --> 15:55.484
Well, what if it tasted like
every bottle had a nickel in it?

16:01.627 --> 16:04.253
I want you to sign my chest.

16:04.263 --> 16:06.922
And I want to hawk a loogie
in your face.

16:08.667 --> 16:11.694
I want you to sign my ass.

16:11.704 --> 16:14.396
And I want to hawk a loogie
in your face.

16:16.575 --> 16:18.701
I want you to autograph my stomach.

16:18.711 --> 16:21.203
Okay, fine, but do me a favor:
don't spit on my friend.

16:21.213 --> 16:22.538
Hey, Brian?

16:22.548 --> 16:24.949
Why don't you mind
your own (BLEEP) business?

16:28.328 --> 16:30.695
Oh, God, again with this Beaglemania?

16:30.705 --> 16:32.681
- Where'd you get those T-shirts?
- From Brian.

16:32.691 --> 16:34.583
He says it's really catching on.

16:34.593 --> 16:37.720
- Well, it isn't. It's a joke.
- It's no joke for him, Dad.

16:37.730 --> 16:40.623
<i>He even recorded The Bite Album.</i>

16:40.633 --> 16:43.359
K-nine. K-nine.

16:43.369 --> 16:47.296
K-nine. K-nine. K-nine.

16:47.306 --> 16:50.109
K-nine. K-nine.

16:53.641 --> 16:55.437
Coming up, uncomfortable pause

16:55.447 --> 16:57.539
as anchor throws to reporter
in the field.

16:57.549 --> 17:01.143
But first, hey, hungover dads,
want to go to a parade?

17:01.153 --> 17:03.412
Does that sound like fun
on a Sunday morning?

17:03.422 --> 17:05.180
Not just being worried about your kids,

17:05.190 --> 17:07.282
but everyone else's kids
around you, too?

17:07.292 --> 17:09.594
For more, here's Tricia Takanawa.

17:13.165 --> 17:14.723
Apparently we've lost Tricia...

17:14.733 --> 17:17.993
Tom, I'm standing here
outside some public toilets

17:18.003 --> 17:20.496
where dads who are really
hurting will be vomiting

17:20.506 --> 17:23.132
in front of their
still-developing children.

17:23.142 --> 17:26.335
The parade is tomorrow,
but already the giant balloons

17:26.345 --> 17:30.272
are being inflated including
two newcomers this year:

17:30.282 --> 17:32.508
Pepe, the alt-right frog,

17:32.518 --> 17:35.844
and Hops the Dog,
the beloved beer pitchman.

17:35.854 --> 17:38.180
Aw, man. Brian gets his own balloon?

17:38.190 --> 17:40.182
This can't get any worse.

17:40.192 --> 17:43.852
In fact, Hops is so popular
that hundreds of Quahog women

17:43.862 --> 17:46.655
have volunteered to blow up his balloon.

17:52.337 --> 17:55.698
Aw, that's the cashier
at the CVS I like.

17:55.708 --> 17:59.034
And here comes the marching band,

17:59.044 --> 18:01.370
led by baton twirler Jane Duncan,

18:01.380 --> 18:04.973
whose aunt is famously-thin
actress Bebe Neuwirth.

18:04.983 --> 18:07.109
Jane lists her hobbies as baton twirling

18:07.119 --> 18:09.545
and trying to contact her aunt.

18:09.555 --> 18:11.547
And, look, is that the beer mascot

18:11.557 --> 18:13.048
you've all been waiting for?

18:13.058 --> 18:16.018
That's right, it's Hops the Dog.

18:16.028 --> 18:19.054
Stupid Brian. Can't even
wave to the crowd right.

18:21.033 --> 18:23.826
Hi! Thanks for coming out. Hi!

18:23.836 --> 18:25.894
Hops! Hops! Hops!

18:25.904 --> 18:29.207
Where's Dad? He's missing this.

18:32.244 --> 18:34.236
Say good-bye, Hops.

18:34.246 --> 18:35.637
Excuse me, sir?

18:35.647 --> 18:37.439
Are you a guest of the hotel?

18:37.449 --> 18:40.109
I-I, uh...
I'm-I'm just here for an event.

18:40.119 --> 18:42.344
Oh, are you part
of Sarah's bridal brunch?

18:42.354 --> 18:43.846
Uh, yeah. Yeah.

18:43.856 --> 18:46.014
Can't-can't believe
she's heading down the aisle.

18:46.024 --> 18:48.350
Well, they're making speeches
in the Santa Fe Lounge.

18:48.360 --> 18:50.528
If you hurry,
you can still get yours in.

18:53.265 --> 18:57.593
Well, Sarah, another turning
point, a fork stuck in the road.

18:57.603 --> 18:58.794
Who is he again?

18:58.804 --> 19:00.896
I think he's that guy from the funeral.

19:00.906 --> 19:02.931
You know, part of me
is glad Sarah met Henry,

19:02.941 --> 19:05.434
because she and I had a pact
that if neither of us

19:05.444 --> 19:07.436
was married by 40, we'd get hitched.

19:07.446 --> 19:10.572
And I think you all know
how that would have gone.

19:12.284 --> 19:14.109
Everybody, get down!

19:21.593 --> 19:23.519
So, to Sarah and Henry.

19:23.529 --> 19:26.155
May they have a long and happy marriage.

19:31.637 --> 19:34.630
Tom, I'm standing here
along the parade route

19:34.640 --> 19:37.299
where the Hops balloon
has just been punctured,

19:37.309 --> 19:39.401
and is now raining helium

19:39.411 --> 19:40.569
Down on the crowd,

19:40.579 --> 19:43.605
creating chaos and wreaking havoc.

19:44.716 --> 19:46.341
We have an active shooter!

19:46.351 --> 19:48.644
I repeat, we have an active shooter!

19:48.654 --> 19:52.323
I can't stress the seriousness
of this situation enough!

19:56.895 --> 19:58.954
This is a disaster!

19:58.964 --> 20:00.455
Brian, you're fired.

20:00.465 --> 20:02.491
What do you mean? This isn't my fault.

20:02.501 --> 20:06.161
I'm never drinking this beer again.

20:06.171 --> 20:08.514
My voice is impervious to helium.

20:20.200 --> 20:21.691
What a mess, huh?

20:21.701 --> 20:24.105
Hey, Peter, sorry all that fame
went to my head.

20:24.115 --> 20:26.083
And I'm sorry I shot your balloon.

20:26.085 --> 20:27.942
How'd you get out of jail so fast?

20:27.952 --> 20:29.611
And I'm sorry II took a hostage...

20:29.621 --> 20:31.613
It's an ongoing situation.

20:33.625 --> 20:36.782
Honey, close that window
and come to bed.

20:36.792 --> 20:38.853
- In a minute.
- Greg Mitchell,

20:38.863 --> 20:42.503
<i>sometimes I feel like
I married you and that window.</i>

20:42.513 --> 20:44.577
The two of you
are more similar than you think.

20:44.587 --> 20:45.952
And how's that?

20:45.962 --> 20:49.297
Well, for one thing,
you're both a real pane.

20:53.745 --> 20:56.413
<i>Window.</i>

20:57.422 --> 21:00.927
Thank you for watching "Bob's Burgers " on
www.FOX-fan.tv